# onnxruntime-node's install script optionally fetches extra platform-specific
# binaries (e.g. GPU acceleration support) from a NuGet feed outside npm's
# registry. We only ever run CPU inference, and that download has been observed
# to fail with ECONNRESET on Elastic Beanstalk's network, breaking `npm install`
# entirely. Skip it — the CPU binaries onnxruntime-node needs are already
# bundled in the package itself.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
